daneman@czech.sw.mcc.com (Michael Daneman) writes:

{M} I was playing nethack the other day and I drank a potion (or maybe I
{M} read a scroll, I don't remember) and it asked me:

You drank a potion.

{M} Make invisibility permanent? [y/n]"  To which I said "yes" and I've been
{M} invisible ever since (although I can still see my character on the screen).
{M} What is this potion/scroll, I've never seen this kind of stuff before?

Why yes.  This was one of the absolute first things that ever happened to
me in 3.0, and I've been wondering about it ever since.

(Spoilers?)

The prompt that you experienced was caused by a blessed potion of
invisibility.

The fact that you could see yourself still was caused by the fact that you
have (somehow) aquired intrinsic see-invisible.
	Elves get this to start.
	Quaffing from a fountain ("You see an image of someone stalking you")
	Or even from a potion of see invisible (tastes like fruit juice).
	There may be more ...

However, my question is:
	You had *no* way of knowing what that potion had done for you (in fact
had the potion been simply uncursed you'd have recieved no message at
all!).  Yet you get prompted.  Should this happen?

	I'd have to say I wouldn't want to see the effects changed (because
I wouldn't want to be screwed out of permanent invisibility just because
I could see invisible), but there's this way doesn't seems quite right
either.

